      "arabic_text": "عَنۡهُ، عَنۡ عَلِيٍّ بِنۡ عَائِذٍ الرَّازِيّ، عَنَ الۡحَسَنِ بِنۡ وَجۡنَاءَ النَّصِيبِيّ، عَنۡ أَبِي نَعِيمٍ مُحَمَّدِ بِنۡ أَحۡمَدَ الۡأَنۡصَارِيّ قَالَ: كُنتُ حَاضِرًا عِندَ الۡمُسۡتَجَارِ بِمَكَّةَ وَجَمۡعَةٌ زَهۡوَا ثَلَاثِينَ رَجُلًا لَمۡ يَكُنۡ مِّنۡهُمۡ مُّخۡلَصٌ غَيۡرُ مُحَمَّدِ بِنۡ الۡقَاسِمِ الۡعَلَوِيّ، فَبَيۡنَمَا نَحۡنُ كَذَٰلِكَ فِي الۡيَوۡمِ الۡسَّادِسِ مِنۡ ذِي الۡحِجَّةِ سَنَةَ ثَلَاثٍ وَتِسۡعِينَ وَمِائَتَيْنِ، إِذۡ خَرَجَ عَلَيۡنَا شَابٌ مِنَ الۡطَوَافِ عَلَيۡهِ إِزَارَانِ مُحۡرِمٌ بِهِمَا، وَفِي يَدِهِ نَعۡلَانِ. فَلَمَّا رَأَيۡنَاهُ قُمۡنَا جَمِيعًا هَيۡبَةً لَهٗ، وَلَمۡ يَبۡقَ مِنۡنَا أَحَدٌ إِلَّا قَامَ، فَسَلَّمَ عَلَيۡنَا وَجَلَسَ مُتَوَسِّطًا وَنَحۡنُ حَوۡلَهٗ، ثُمَّ التَفَتَ يَمِينًا وَشِمَالًا ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَتَدۡرُونَ مَا كَانَ أَبُوۡ عَبۡدِاللَّهِ عَلَيۡهِ الۡسَّلَامُ يَقُولُ فِي دُعَاءِ الۡإِلۡحَاحِ؟ (قُلۡنَا: وَمَا كَانَ يَقُولُ؟) قَالَ: كَانَ يَقُولُ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّيۡ أَسۡأَلُكَ بِاسۡمِكَ الَّذِي بِهِ تَقُومُ الۡسَّمَاءُ، وَبِهِ تَقُومُ الۡأَرۡضُ وَبِهِ تَفۡرَقُ بَيۡنَ الۡحَقِّ وَالۡبَاطِلِ، وَبِهِ تَجۡمَعُ بَيۡنَ الۡمُتَفَرِّقِ، وَبِهِ تَفۡرَقُ بَيۡنَ الۡمُجۡتَمِعِ، وَبِهِ أَحۡصَيۡتَ عَدَدَ الۡرِمَالِ، وَزَنَةَ الۡجِبَالِ، وَكِيلَ الۡبِحَارِ، أَنۡ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ، وَأَنۡ تَجۡعَلَ لِي مِنۡ أَمۡرِي فَرَجًا. ثُمَّ نَهَضَ وَدَخَلَ الۡطَوَافَ فَقُمۡنَا لِقِيَامِهِ حَتَّىٰ انصَرَفَ وَأَنۡسَيْنَا أَنۡ نَذۡكُرَهٗ أَمۡرَهٗ، وَأَنۡ نَقُولَ مَنۡ هُوَ؟ وَأَيُّ شَيۡءٍ هُوَ؟ إِلَى الۡغَدِ فِي ذَٰلِكَ الۡوَقۡتِ فَخَرَجَ عَلَيۡنَا مِنَ الۡطَوَافِ، فَقُمۡنَا لَهٗ كَقِيَامِنَا بِالۡأَمۡسِ، وَجَلَسَ فِي مَجۡلِسِهِ مُتَوَسِّطًا، فَنَظَرَ يَمِينًا وَشِمَالًا وَقَالَ: أَتَدۡرُونَ مَا كَانَ يَقُولُ أَمِيرُ الۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ عَلَيۡهِ الۡسَّلَامُ بَعۡدَ صَلَاةِ الۡفَرِيضَةِ؟ فَقُلۡنَا: وَمَا كَانَ يَقُولُ؟ قَالَ: كَانَ يَقُولُ: إِلَيۡكَ رَفَعَتِ الۡأَصۡوَٰتُ (وَدُعِيَتِ الۡدَعَوَاتُ وَلَك) عَنَتِ الۡوُجُوهُ، وَلَكَ وَضَعَتِ الۡرِقَابُ، وَإِلَيۡكَ الۡتِحَاكُمُ فِي الۡأَعۡمَالِ، يَا خَيۡرَ مَنۡ سُئِلَ، وَيَا خَيۡرَ مَنۡ أُعۡطِي، يَا صَادِقُ يَا بَارِئُ، يَا مَنۡ لَا يُخۡلِفُ الۡمِيعَادَ، يَا مَنۡ أَمَرَ بِالدُّعَاءِ وَوَعَدَ بِالۡإِجَابَةِ، يَا مَنۡ قَالَ: ﴿اُدۡعُونِيۡ أَسۡتَجِبۡ لَكُمۡ﴾ يَا مَنۡ قَالَ: ﴿إِذَا سَأَلَكَ عِبَادِي عَنِّي فَإِنِّي قَرِيبٌ أُجِيبُ دَعۡوَةَ الۡدَاعِ إِذَا دَعَانِي فَلۡيَسۡتَجِيبُوا لِي وَلۡيُؤۡمِنُوا بِي لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَرۡشُدُونَ﴾ وَيَا مَنۡ قَالَ: ﴿يَا عِبَادِيَ الَّذِينۡ أَسۡرَفُوا عَلَىٰ أَنۡفُسِهِمۡ لَا تَقۡنَطُوا مِنۡ رَحۡمَةِ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَغۡفِرُ الۡذُنُوبَ جَمِيعًا إِنَّهُ هُوَ الۡغَفُورُ الرَّحِيمُ﴾ لَبَّيۡكَ وَسَعۡدَيۡكَ، هَٰنَا ذَا بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡكَ الۡمُسۡرِفُ، وَأَنتَ الۡقَائِلُ: ﴿لَا تَقۡنَطُوا مِنۡ رَحۡمَةِ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَغۡفِرُ الۡذُنُوبَ جَمِيعًا﴾. ثُمَّ نَظَرَ يَمِينًا وَشِمَالًا بَعۡدَ هَٰذَا الدُّعَاءِ فَقَالَ: أَتَدۡرُونَ مَا كَانَ أَمِيرُ الۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ عَلَيۡهِ الۡسَّلَامُ يَقُولُ فِي سَجۡدَةِ الۡشُّكۡرِ؟ فَقُلۡنَا: وَمَا كَانَ يَقُولُ؟ قَالَ: كَانَ يَقُولُ: يَا مَنۡ لَا يَزِيدُهُ كَثۡرَةُ الدُّعَاءِ إِلَّا سَعَةً وَوَعۡطًا، يَا مَنۡ لَا تَنۡفَدُ خَزَٰئِنُهٗ، يَا مَنۡ لَهٗ خَزَٰئِنُ الۡسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَالۡأَرۡضِ، يَا مَنۡ لَهٗ خَزَٰئِنُ مَا دَقَّ وَجَلَّ لَا تَمۡنَعۡكَ إِسَٰٓءَتِي مِنۡ إِحۡسَانِكَ، أَنتَ تَفۡعَلُ بِي الَّذِي أَنتَ أَهۡلُهٗ، (فَإِنَّكَ) أَنتَ أَهۡلُ الۡكَرَمِ وَالۡجُودِ، وَالۡعَفۡوِ وَالۡتَجَاوُزِ، يَا رَبِّ يَا اللَّهُ لَا تَفۡعَلۡ بِي الَّذِي أَنَا أَهۡلُهٗ، فَإِنِّيۡ أَهۡلُ الۡعُقُوبَةِ وَقَدِ اسۡتَحۡقَقۡتُهَا، لَا حُجَّةَ (لِي) وَلَا عَذۡرَ لِي عِندَكَ، أَبُوءُ لَكَ بِذُنُوبِي جَمِيعًا وَأَعۡتَرِفُ بِهَا كَيۡ تَعۡفُوَ عَنِّي، وَأَنتَ أَعۡلَمُ بِهَا مِنِّي، أَبُوءُ لَكَ بِكُلِّ ذَنۢبٍ أَذۡنَبۡتُهٗ، وَكُلِّ خَطِيۡئَةٍ احۡتَمَلۡتُهَا، وَكُلِّ سَيِّئَةٍ عَمِلۡتُهَا، رَبِّ اغۡفِرۡ وَارۡحَمۡ، وَتَجَاوَزۡ عَمَّا تَعۡلَمُ، إِنَّكَ أَنتَ الۡأَعَزُّ الۡأَكۡرَمُ. وَقَامَ وَدَخَلَ الۡطَوَافَ فَقُمۡنَا لِقِيَامِهِ، وَعَادَ مِنَ الۡغَدِ فِي ذَٰلِكَ الۡوَقۡتِ فَقُمۡنَا لِإِقۡبَالِهِ كَفَعۡلِنَا فِيمَا مَضَىٰ، فَجَلَسَ مُتَوَسِّطًا وَنَظَرَ يَمِينًا وَشِمَالًا فَقَالَ: كَانَ عَلِيٌّ بِنُ الۡحُسَيۡنِ سَيِّدُ الۡعَابِدِينَ عَلَيۡهِ الۡسَّلَامُ يَقُولُ فِي سَجۡودِهِ فِي هَٰذَا الۡمَوۡضِعِ -وَإِشَارَةٌ بِيَدِهِ إِلَى الۡحَجَرِ تَحۡتَ الۡمِيزَابِ-: عَبِيدُكَ بِفِنَائِكَ مَسۡكِينُكَ بِفِنَائِكَ، فَقِيرُكَ بِفِنَائِكَ، سَٰٓئِلُكَ بِفِنَائِكَ يَسۡأَلُكَ مَا لَا يَقۡدِرُ عَلَيۡهِ غَيۡرُكَ. ثُمَّ نَظَرَ يَمِينًا وَشِمَالًا وَنَظَرَ إِلَى مُحَمَّدِ بِنۡ الۡقَاسِمِ مِنۡ بَيۡنِنَا، فَقَالَ: يَا مُحَمَّدَ بِنَ الۡقَاسِمِ أَنتَ عَلَىٰ خَيۡرٍ إِنۡ شَآءَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَىٰ -وَكَانَ مُحَمَّدُ بِنُ الۡقَاسِمِ يَقُولُ بِهَٰذَا الۡأَمۡرِ- ثُمَّ قَامَ وَدَخَلَ الۡطَوَافَ فَمَا بَقِيَ مِنۡنَا أَحَدٌ إِلَّا وَقَدۡ أُلۡهِمَ مَا ذَكَرَهٗ مِنَ الدُّعَاءِ وَأَنۡسَيۡنَا أَنۡ نَتَذَاكَرُ أَمۡرًا إِلَّا فِي آخِرِ يَوۡمٍ. فَقَالَ لَنَا أَبُو عَلِيٍّ الۡمَحۡمُودِيّ: يَا قَوۡمَ أَتَعۡرِفُونَ هَٰذَا؟ هَٰذَا وَاللَّهِ صَاحِبُ زَمَانِكُمۡ، فَقُلۡنَا: وَكَيۡفَ عَلِمۡتَ يَا أَبَا عَلِيٍّ؟ فَذَكَرَ أَنَّهُ مَكَثَ سَبۡعَ سَنَوَاتٍ يَدۡعُو رَبَّهٗ وَيَسۡأَلُهٗ مُعَانَاةَ صَاحِبِ الۡزَّمَانِ عَلَيۡهِ الۡسَّلَامُ. قَالَ: فَبَيۡنَمَا نَحۡنُ يَوۡمًا عَشِيَّةَ عَرَفَةَ وَإِذَا بِالرَّجُلِ بِعَيۡنِهِ يَدۡعُو بِدُعَآءٍ عَوَّتَهٗ فَسَأَلۡتُهٗ مَنۡ هُوَ؟ فَقَالَ: مِنَ الۡنَّاسِ، قُلۡتُ: مِنۡ أَيِّ النَّاسِ؟ قَالَ: مِنۡ عَرَبِهَا، قُلۡتُ: مِنۡ أَيِّ عَرَبِهَا؟ قَالَ: مِنۡ أَشۡرَفِهَا، قُلۡتُ: وَمَنۡ هُمۡ؟ قَالَ: بَنُو هَٰشِمٍ، قُلۡتُ: (و) مِنۡ أَيِّ بَنِي هَٰشِمٍ؟ فَقَالَ: مِنۡ أَعۡلَاهَا ذَرۡوَةً وَأَسۡنَاهَا، قُلۡتُ: مِمَّنۡ؟ قَالَ: مِمَّنۡ فَلَقَ الۡهَامَ وَأَطۡعَمَ الۡطَعَامَ وَصَلَّىٰ وَالنَّاسُ نِيَامٌ. قَالَ: فَعَلِمۡتُ أَنَّهُ عَلَوِيٌّ فَأَحۡبَبۡتُهٗ عَلَى الۡعَلَوِيَّةِ، ثُمَّ افۡتَقَدۡتُهٗ مِنۡ بَيۡنِ يَدَيَّ فَلَمۡ أَدۡرِ كَيۡفَ مَضَىٰ، فَسَأَلۡتُ الۡقَوۡمَ الَّذِين كَانُوا حَوۡلَهٗ تَعۡرِفُونَ هَٰذَا الۡعَلَوِيَّ؟ قَالُوا: نَعَمۡ يَحُجُّ مَعَنَا فِي كُلِّ سَنَةٍ مَّاشِيًا، فَقُلۡتُ: سُبۡحَانَ اللَّهِ (وَاللَّه) مَا أَرَىٰ بِهِۦ أَثَرَ مَشۡيٍ قَالَ: فَانصَرَفۡتُ إِلَى الۡمُزۡدَلِفَةِ كَئِيبًا حَزِينًا عَلَىٰ فِرَاقِهٖ، وَنَمۡتُ مِنۡ لَيۡلَتِي تِلۡكَ، فَإِذَا أَنَا بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِ وَآلِهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا أَحۡمَدُ رَأَيۡتَ طَلَبَتَكَ؟ فَقُلۡتُ: وَمَنۡ ذَٰلِكَ يَا سَيِّدِي؟ فَقَالَ: الَّذِي رَأَيۡتَهٗ فِي عَشِيَّتِكَ (و) هُوَ صَاحِبُ زَمَانِكَ. قَالَ: فَلَمَّا سَمِعۡنَا ذَٰلِكَ مِنۡهُ عَتَبۡنَاهُ أَنۡ لَا يَكُونَ عَلَمَنَا ذَٰلِكَ، فَذَكَرَ أَنَّهُ كَانَ يَنۡسَىٰ أَمۡرَهٗ إِلَىٰ وَقۡتٍ مَّا حَدَّثَنَا بِهِ.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "From him, from Ali ibn A'yyash al-Razi, from al-Hasan ibn Wajna al-Nasibi, from Abu Nu'aym Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Ansari who said: I was present near the Mushtar (spout) in Mecca with a group of about thirty men, among whom there was no one sincere (in faith) except Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Alawi. While we were in that state on the sixth day of Dhu al-Hijjah in the year 293 AH, a young man came out from the Tawaf upon him were two izar (garments), wearing Ihram with them, and in his hand were two sandals. When we saw him, we all stood out of awe for him, and none of us remained but that he stood. He greeted us and sat in the middle while we were around him. Then he looked to the right and left and said: Do you know what Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him) used to say in the supplication of Al-Haḥ? We said: And what did he say? He said: He used to say: O Allah, I ask You by Your name by which the sky stands, and by which the earth stands, and by which truth and falsehood are distinguished, and by which the scattered are gathered, and by which the cohesive are dispersed, and by which the number of sands, the weight of mountains, and the measure of seas are counted, that You send prayer upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and that You make for me a way out of my affair. Then he rose and entered the Tawaf, and we stood for his rising until he departed, and we forgot to ask him about his affair, and to say: Who is he? And what is he? Until the next day at that time he came out to us from the Tawaf, and we stood for him as we stood yesterday, and he sat in his seat in the middle, so he looked right and left and said: Do you know what Amir al-Mu'minin (peace be upon him) used to say after the obligatory prayer? We said: And what did he say? He said: He used to say: To You were raised the voices (and were called the supplications), and to You were bowed the faces, and to You were placed the necks, and to You is referred the judgment in the deeds, O best of those who are asked, and O best of those who are given, O Truthful, O Creator, O He who does not break the promise, O He who commanded supplication and promised response, O He who said: 'Call upon Me, I will respond to you,' O He who said: 'When My servants ask you concerning Me, then indeed I am near; I answer the supplication of the suppliant when he calls on Me, so let them respond to My call and believe in Me that they may be guided,' and O He who said: 'O My servants who have acted extravagantly against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah; indeed Allah forgives the sins all together; indeed He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.' To Your call and my happiness, here I am before You, the extravagant, and You are the One who said: 'Do not despair of the mercy of Allah; indeed Allah forgives the sins all together.' Then he looked right and left after this supplication and said: Do you know what Amir al-Mu'minin (peace be upon him) used to say in the prostration of gratitude? We said: And what did he say? He said: He used to say: O He who does not increase His abundance of supplication except with generosity and giving, O He whose treasuries do not run out, O He to whom belong the treasuries of the heavens and the earth, O He to whom belong the treasuries of what is small and great, do not withhold Your kindness from me because of my misdeeds, You do to me what befits You, (for indeed) You are the worthy of generosity and bounty, and forgiveness and pardon, O Lord, O Allah, do not do to me what I deserve, for I am worthy of punishment and I have earned it, I have no argument (for myself) nor excuse before You, I confess to You for all my sins and acknowledge them so that You may forgive me, and You are more knowing of them than I, I confess to You for every sin I committed, and every mistake I made, and every evil deed I did, O Lord, forgive and have mercy, and overlook what You know, for indeed You are the Most Mighty, the Most Generous. And he rose and entered the Tawaf, and we stood for his rising, and he returned the next day at that time, and we stood for his approach as we did before, and he sat in the middle and looked right and left and said: Ali ibn al-Husayn, the Master of the Worshippers (peace be upon him) used to say in his prostration in this place -and he pointed with his hand to the Stone under the spout-: Your slaves are at Your threshold, Your poor are at Your door, Your beggar is at Your door, he asks You for what none other can do. Then he looked right and left and looked at Muhammad ibn al-Qasim from among us, and said: O Muhammad ibn al-Qasim, you are upon good, if Allah wills -and Muhammad ibn al-Qasim used to say with this matter- Then he rose and entered the Tawaf, and none of us remained but that he was inspired with what he mentioned of the supplication, and we forgot to discuss his matter except on the last day. So Abu Ali al-Mahmudi said to us: O people, do you know this? This is, by Allah, the Master of your time. We said: And how did you know, O Abu Ali? He mentioned that he spent seven years calling upon his Lord and asking Him for the sighting of the Master of the Age (peace be upon him). He said: While we were one day in the afternoon of Arafah, and behold the man with his own eyes was supplicating with a supplication he had memorized, so I asked him: Who is he? He said: From the people. I said: From which people? He said: From its Arabs. I said: From which of its Arabs? He said: From its most noble. I said: And who are they? He said: Banu Hashim. I said: And from which of Banu Hashim? He said: From its highest peak and its loftiest. I said: From whom? He said: From him who split the head (of the blind), fed the food, and prayed while the people were sleeping. He said: So I knew that he was Alawi, so I loved him for the Alawiyyah. Then I missed him from before me and did not know how he passed, so I asked the people who were around him: Do you know this Alawi? They said: Yes, he performs Hajj with us every year walking. I said: Glory be to Allah (and by Allah) I do not see in him the effect of walking. He said: So I returned to Muzdalifah sad and sorrowful over his parting, and I slept from that night, and behold I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) who said: O Ahmad, have you seen your desire? I said: And who is that, O my master? He said: The one you saw in your afternoon (and) he is the Master of your time. He said: When we heard that from him, we reproached him that he did not inform us of that, so he mentioned that he used to forget his matter until the time he told us about it."
